Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:08:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1428/1463] HERESY 1489: Content Credentials (C2PA) on the
 downloads; the switch and the fields in Engine
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every download of a take or of a file of its tree (WAV, FLAC, MP3) and each audio file of the Library's ZIP carries a signed record of its origin: made by AI (YuE2) in Ruach Studio; refined by a person, with the Refiner's steps, when the Refiner made it; the author and the site or contact given in Engine. The sound is not touched. The lab signs on the way (GET /c2pa/file, the engine's own file in from=), with the install's own certificate made at first use, or a certificate and key of one's own (PEM). A take imported from elsewhere goes out as it came; a download asked to be signed that cannot be fails out loud. Engine › Folders and Security: the switch, Author, Site or contact, Your certificate, Its key, and what signs now. c2pa_sign.py, test_c2pa.py; requirements: c2pa-python 0.38, cryptography.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
